Docker Containerization — Steps
1. Open Docker Desktop and wait until it is running.
2. Verify Docker: On cmd or powershell
   docker --version
   docker compose version
3. Clone the project:
   git clone https://github.com/docker/getting-started-todo-app
4. Navigate to the project directory:
   cd getting-started-todo-app
5. Start the application:
   docker compose watch
6. Open a second terminal and check containers:
   docker compose ps
7. Build the Docker image:
   docker build -t welcome .
8. Verify the image:
   docker images
9. Open the application in the browser:
   http://localhost:3000
10. Verify the application is running in the browser.
